Chapter: ProbeRealApproxBits

 The f32 half of the approx-equality probe, held apart from
 probe-approx-eq.codex because today it cannot run: the zig plug has no
 emitter for `bits-to-real-approx`, so this chapter transpiles to three
 `@compileError` markers and the unit refuses. A refusal is the lucky case
 -- the defect it would otherwise demonstrate (IrApproxEq emitted as `==`,
 dropping bare metal's 4-ULP band) produces a wrong answer, not an error --
 but the missing emitter blocks the demonstration, and is itself a gap
 worth an entry.

 Once bits-to-real-approx emits, this is the sharper instrument: the bit
 patterns are pinned, #3F800000 and #3F800001 are one ULP apart by
 definition, and the f32 path exercises emit-approx-eq's width flag, which
 the f64 probe cannot.

 Expected on bare metal:

   one-ulp 1
   same 1
   five-ulp 0

 A plug that emits == prints one-ulp 0. A plug without the builtin refuses
 with `zig plug: no emitter for bits-to-real-approx`, which is what it does
 today.

Section: Values

  a0 : Real approximate
  a0 = bits-to-real-approx #3F800000

  a1 : Real approximate
  a1 = bits-to-real-approx #3F800001

  a5 : Real approximate
  a5 = bits-to-real-approx #3F800005

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("one-ulp " & show (if a0 ~ a1 then 1 else 0))
    print-line-uni ("same " & show (if a0 ~ a0 then 1 else 0))
    print-line-uni ("five-ulp " & show (if a0 ~ a5 then 1 else 0))
  end
